### ChurnScope API smoke tests
### Requires: API running on localhost:8000, seeded + backfilled data
###
### Usage in VS Code: install "REST Client" extension, then click "Send Request"
### above each block. Alternatively pipe to httpie or curl equivalents.

@host = http://localhost:8000

### Health
GET {{host}}/health

### Recompute scores for today
POST {{host}}/api/scores/recompute

### Backfill 30 days of scores
POST {{host}}/api/scores/backfill?days=30

### Dashboard summary
GET {{host}}/api/dashboard/summary

### List all interpreters (paginated)
GET {{host}}/api/interpreters?limit=25

### Filter to Red band, Spanish speakers
GET {{host}}/api/interpreters?band=red&language=es&limit=50

### Filter to interpreters silent for 7+ days
GET {{host}}/api/interpreters?max_days_since_last_session=7

### One interpreter detail (paste an id from the list response)
# GET {{host}}/api/interpreters/{{id}}

### Timeline for an interpreter
# GET {{host}}/api/interpreters/{{id}}/timeline?days=30

### List interventions
GET {{host}}/api/interventions

### Create an intervention
# POST {{host}}/api/interventions
# Content-Type: application/json
#
# {
#   "interpreter_id": "PASTE-UUID-HERE",
#   "action": "coach_call",
#   "notes": "Morning check-in"
# }

### Ingest 1 interpreter (illustrative)
POST {{host}}/api/ingest/interpreters
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "items": [
    {
      "external_id": "smoke-1",
      "full_name": "Smoke Test",
      "languages": ["en", "es"],
      "certifications": [],
      "hired_at": "2025-01-01",
      "status": "active"
    }
  ]
}
